    "observation": "After exact lexical lookup returned no type, infer_variable_type_cached split every source line, reparsed matching right-hand-side fragments with Prism, ignored lexical and hard method boundaries, and returned the first same-named assignment in the file. This repeated parsing and created semantically invalid receiver ownership."
  },
  "change": {
    "implementation": "A LocalVariableRead receiver now returns only FactCollector::get_local_var_type at its exact source location. The collector-local OnceCell<HashMap<String, RubyType>>, infer_variable_type_cached, and build_variable_type_map were removed.",
    "semantic_boundary": "VariableScopes remains the sole local-variable authority. It walks capturable soft block parents, stops at hard method/class boundaries, and considers only assignments preceding the receiver. No file-wide text scan or nested Prism parse may recover an unknown local receiver.",
    "failure_policy": "When no defensible lexical fact exists, receiver inference returns None and downstream method attribution fails closed."
  },
  "red_green": {
    "test": "local_receiver_inference_does_not_borrow_an_assignment_from_another_method",
    "fixture": "class User; end; def inspect(user); user.save; end; def build; user = User.new; end",
    "red": "The old fallback incorrectly emitted User as the owner of save for the untyped inspect parameter by borrowing build's later assignment.",
    "green": "No owner is emitted for save. The existing captured-block regression still resolves outer User#save and nested String#upcase with zero global scope scans.",
